{"page": 49, "text": "Net Sales During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, net sales were $5,243.3 million, an increase of $133.4 million, or 2.6%, as compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025, primarily due to an increase in sales attributable to our premium brands of $82.2 million and regional spring water of $68.9 million, partially offset by a decrease of $21.7 million related to the exited US office coffee services business. Cost of Sales During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, cost of sales was $3,675.8 million, an increase of $156.0 million, or 4.4%, as compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025. The increase in costs was primarily due to increased transportation related costs of $105.9 million, increased materials costs of $33.0 million, and increased depreciation and amortization of $26.1 million, partially offset by a decrease in non-recurring integration related costs incurred in the current year period of $23.4 million and a decrease of $18.7 million related to the exited US office coffee services business. Gross Profit and Gross Margin During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, gross profit was $1,567.5 million, a decrease of $22.6 million, or 1.4%, as compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025, and gross margin as a percentage of net sales was 29.9%, as compared to 31.1% during the nine months ended September 30, 2025, primarily driven by the factors discussed above. 39 Table of Contents Selling, General and Administrative Expenses During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, selling, general and administrative expenses were $998.5 million, a decrease of $50.9 million, or 4.9%, as compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025, primarily due to a decrease in marketing costs of $25.8 million and a decrease in depreciation and amortization of $33.6 million primarily related to the amortization of definite lived intangibles in the prior year period not recurring in the current year period. Acquisition, Integration and Restructuring Expenses During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, acquisition, integration and restructuring expenses were $47.5 million, a decrease of $86.2 million, as compared to the nine months ended September 30, 2025, primarily due to lower integration costs as integration efforts begin to wind down as well as net restructuring gains in the current year period. Other Operating Income, Net During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, other operating income, net was $45.7 million, compared to $5.4 million during the nine months ended September 30, 2025. This change is primarily due to unrealized gains on commodity forwards of $46.5 million during the nine months ended September 30, 2026 compared to unrealized gains on commodity forwards of $3.8 million in the prior year period.\n"}
